  "problem": "Given $Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))$, we reduce $Q$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $5$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))=0.\n$$",
